/-!
# §7.1: Proposition 7.3 (trace part) and its one-force seed case, in the forms the κ < 4 induction uses

Packet PROVE-SEC7-A4. Specification §7.1 (`source/spec/p241-288.md` L38–L44, p. 242):

> **Proposition 7.3.** Let `0 < κ < 4` and `ρ^L, ρ^R > −2`. The integrated `SLE_κ(ρ^L; ρ^R)` process with force
> points at `0⁻, 0⁺` is generated by a continuous simple curve that tends to `∞` as its capacity tends to `∞`. […]
>
> *Proof.* The embedded construction has produced one pair in which the field determines the curve, with the
> canonical retained-range kernels. Integrated driving uniqueness transfers its continuous simple trace and
> transience to the stated two-seed driving law. Since both seed weights exceed `−2`, that evolution has infinite
> lifetime.

and p. 378 (`source/spec/p337-384.md` L843–L875): "The one-force seed case is part of that theorem".

The κ < 4 induction (`Sec7.revisedInductionLtFourStatement_of_inputs`, PROVE-SEC7-C2) uses Proposition 7.3 in the
forms `Sec7.Prop73TraceStatement` and `Sec7.SeedOneForceTraceStatement`. This file proves both from the embedded
reference of Lemma 7.1 and two further named inputs:

* `prop73TraceStatement_of_inputs`: **Proposition 7.3, trace part**, from one reference evolution per admissible
  pair (Lemma 7.1, `Lemma71TraceReferenceStatement`), the measurable coding of the transient-trace event
  (`TransientTraceCodingStatement`) and the existence of the Jacobi diffusion (`JacobiDiffusionExistsStatement`, for
  the infinite two-seed lifetime). The transfer is Theorem 2.2's two-seed uniqueness (`ae_transfer_of_coding`).
* `seedOneForceTraceStatement_of_prop73`: **the one-force seed case from Proposition 7.3**. A mark of weight `0` at
  the empty side is added by taking a two-seed evolution with weights `(0; ρ)` (Theorem 2.2's existence), whose trace
  Proposition 7.3 supplies; forgetting the zero mark gives a one-mark evolution with that trace, and Theorem 2.2's
  one-force uniqueness transfers it to every one-mark evolution. The left seed follows by reflection.
* `transientTraceCodingStatement_of_top`: the transience part of the coding (a countable condition on the measurable
  trace evaluations `LP.traceAt` at rational times, read off the rational values through `extendRat`);
* `prop73TraceStatement_of_lemma71`, `seedOneForceTraceStatement_of_lemma71`: both forms from the trace-only coding;
* `revisedInductionLtFourStatement_of_lemma71`: the κ < 4 induction with these two inputs discharged.

## Named inputs

| Input | Source |
|---|---|
| `Lemma71TraceReferenceStatement` | Lemma 7.1 (p. 223) with p. 227 ("the embedded construction therefore covers every admissible two-seed pair") |
| `TopTraceCodingStatement` | Corollary LP11's measurable trace reconstruction (pp. 488–489) and Aux. 126's coding (pp. 399–400); its transience upgrade `TransientTraceCodingStatement` is proved (`transientTraceCodingStatement_of_top`) |
| `JacobiDiffusionExistsStatement` | Theorem 2.2's proof (p. 23), already a named input of PROVE-SEC7-D2 |
-/

